                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Short version: 86%[/h1]\nThanks to an unconventional storyline about a chaotic family drama and some wonderful hidden object scenes, Blood Ruby is a great addition to the HOG genre, despite its tendency to overuse point ‘n’ click components.\n\n[h1]Long version:[/h1]\nSaving a relative is a common theme in hidden object games. Travelling back in time to end up in a murder investigation that eventually leads to a surprisingly messed-up and bloody domestic feud… well, that takes it several steps beyond expected levels. \n\nDark Cases: The Blood Ruby has more than just this memorable plot—or similarly memorable beautiful artwork, for that matter. It is a roughly three-hour joyride with some pacing bumps and a few outlandish elements, elevating its murder mystery far above similar casual detective stories.\n\nAdmittedly, the game relies on these elements to keep the players invested, because it is a bit too keen on relying on classic adventure game methods, including a perpetually overcrowded inventory. The hidden object scenes are great, but too few to turn The Blood Ruby into the truly unforgettable HOG masterpiece its story would deserve.",
